       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 4250 mg three times daily comes to 12,750 mg/day, which is five times the FDA maximum for metformin (2,550 mg/day). The usual maximum single dose is 1,000 mg. A dose this high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis.\n\nThis may be a typo. Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day), the usual maximum\n- **425 mg TID**, though metformin doesn't come in that strength\n- **1,000 mg BID** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **500 mg TID** (1,500 mg/day)\n\nIf you really do want 4250 mg per dose, please confirm that explicitly and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it's intentional. Otherwise, tell me the dose you meant and I'll enter it now."
