     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 12,750 mg/day of metformin has no therapeutic use. It is in the range associated with metformin-induced lactic acidosis, which can be fatal. That risk is higher in acute overdose, and this dose would be given every day. Normal kidney and liver function lowers the risk but doesn't make it safe.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Metformin 850 mg PO TID with meals (2,550 mg/day, the labeled maximum)\n- Metformin 1,000 mg PO BID with meals\n- Metformin 500 mg PO TID with meals\n- A lower starting dose, such as 500 mg PO BID with meals, titrated up\n\nIf you have a specific clinical reason for going above the labeled maximum, please talk to pharmacy first and have them verify it. I can enter an order after that review, or I can enter a lower dose now."
      }
     ],
